          %h2#on_lie_groups On Lie groups
          %h3#idea Idea
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %em Maurer-Cartan form
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-algebra+valued+1-form"} Lie-algebra valued 1-form
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %h3#definition_in_synthetic_differential_geometry Definition in synthetic differential geometry
          %p
            Speaking in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            the Maurer-Cartan form has the following definition:
          %p
            any two points
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in G
            are related by a unique group element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta(x,y)
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y = x \cdot \theta(x,y)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+space"} infinitesimally close
            points, defining a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vector"} tangent vector
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta(x,y)
            is an element of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            restricted to infinitesimally close points is a
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          %h3#analytic_definition Analytic definition
          %p
            In terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analysis"} analysis
            there is a direct analogue of this definition: a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vector"} tangent vector
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G
            may be identified with an equivalence class of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma : [0,1] \to G
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma(0) = g
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = e
            are canonically identified with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            back to the origin
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi γ
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^{-1}\gamma : [0,1] \to G \stackrel{g^{-1} \cdot(-)}{\to} G
            it represents a Lie algebra element. This map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\theta := g^{-1}_* : [\gamma] \mapsto [g^{-1} \gamma]
          %p of tangent vectors to Lie algebra elements is the Maurer-Cartan form.
          %p
            If we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : G \to G
            for the identity function on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d g : T G \to T G
            is the identity function on the tangent vectors of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi d
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi e
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g^{-1}_* d g : T G \to T_e G = \mathfrak{g}
                  \\,.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+Lie+group"} matrix Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^{-1}_*
            is literally just left-multiplication of matrices and therefore the Maurer-Cartan form is often written just
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi d
                  %mi g
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\theta = g^{-1} d g
                  \\,.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#curvature Curvature
          %p
            The Maurer-Cartan form is a Lie-algebra valued form with vanishing
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi θ
                  %mo +
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi θ
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d \theta + \frac{1}{2}[\theta \wedge \theta] = 0
          %p
            This is known as the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+equation"} Maurer-Cartan equation
          %p
            Synthetically this is just a restatement of the fact that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in G
            there is a
            %em unique
            group element such that
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y = x \cdot g
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi θ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mrow
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi θ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi y
                              %mo ,
                              %mi z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi θ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; y
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\theta}(x,y)}\nearrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{\theta}(y,z)}
                  \\\
                  x &amp;&amp;\stackrel{\theta(x,z)}{\to}&amp;&amp; z
                  }
          %p
            i.e.
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta(x,y) \theta(y,z) = \theta(x,z)
          %h3#pullback Pullback
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h : X \to G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            with values in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+form"} pullback form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %mi θ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  h^* \theta \in \Omega^1(X,\mathfrak{g})
          %p
            of the Maurer-Cartan form on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^{-1}
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^{-1}_*
            this is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %mi θ
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi d
                  %mi h
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  h^* \theta = h^{-1} d h
                  \\,.
          %p
            Now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi h
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d h : T X \to T G
            is no longer (necessarily) the identity map as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            was when we wrote
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi d
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta = g^{-1} d g
            above, but the form of this equation shows why it can be useful to think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            itself in terms of the identity map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi T
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d g : T G \to T G
          %h3#gauge_transformations Gauge transformations
          %p
            The Maurer-Cartan form crucially appears in the formula for the gauge transformation of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-algebra+valued+1-form"} Lie-algebra valued 1-form
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u : \mathbb{R} \to G
            a smooth function and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \Omega^1(\mathbb{R}, \mathfrak{g})
            a Lie-algebra valued form, the condition that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            is
            %em flat
            with respect to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is that it satisfies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equation"} differential equation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi u
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mi u
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d u = -(R_u)_* \circ A
          %p
            (where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            denotes the right multiplication action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on itself). This is such that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            happens to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+Lie+group"} matrix Lie group
            it is equivalent to
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo +
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi u
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (d + A) u = 0
                  \\,.
          %p
            We call the unique solution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            of this differential equation that satisfies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u(0) = e
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and write it
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo =
                    %mi P
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u = P \exp\big(\int_0^{(-)} A\big)
          %p
            Now for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon \mathbb{R} \to G
            a function, the
            %em gauge transformed
            parallel transport is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi P
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi g
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g^{-1} P \exp(\int_0^{(-)} A) g
                  \\,.
          %p
            This solves a differential equation as above, but for a different 1-form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A'
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ′
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Ad
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A' = Ad_{g^{-1}} A + g^* \theta
          %p or equivalently, with adopted notation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ′
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi A
                  %mi g
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi d
                  %mi g
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A' = g^{-1}A g + g^{-1} d g
                  \\,.
          %h3#InCoordinatesUnderExponentialMap In coordinates under the exponential map
          %p
            Any choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g} \;\simeq\; \mathbb{R}\big\langle (T_i)_{i \in I} \big\rangle
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            of the given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            induces linear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+functions"} coordinate functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x^i)_{i \in I}
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x^i T_i \,\in\, \mathfrak{g}
          %p
            (where we use the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+summation+convention"} Einstein summation convention
            throughout). In terms of these coordinates, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+differential+forms"} pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e^i)_{i \in I}
            of the Maurer-Cartan form along the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+map"} exponential map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} exp \,\colon\, \mathfrak{g} \longrightarrow G
            at any point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = x^i T_i
            is (by
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Schur1891"} Schur 1891 (36)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Helgason01"} Helgason 2001 Thm. 7.4
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Meinrenken13"} Meinrenken 2013 Thm. C.2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %mi exp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi ad
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi ad
                        %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  e^i
                  \\;=\;
                  \\mathrm{d}x^i
                  \\left(
                  \\frac
                  {1 - exp(- ad X)}
                  {ad X}
                  (\partial_k)
                  \\right)
                  \\mathrm{d}x^k
          %p
            where (by
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Helgason01"} Helgason p. 36
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Meinrenken13"} Meinrenken p. 99
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{1 - exp(-A)}{ A }
                  \\;\;
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\;\;
                  \\sum_{n=0}^\infty
                  \\tfrac{1}{(n+1)!}
                  (-A)^n
          %p
            (for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \colon \mathfrak{g} \to \mathfrak{g}
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                          %mn ∞
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo !
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi ad
                      %mi X
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  e^i
                  \\;=\;
                  \\mathrm{d}x^i
                  \\left(
                  \\textstyle{
                  \\sum_{n = 0}^\infty
                  }
                  \\tfrac{1}{(n+1)!}
                  (
                  \- ad X
                  )^n
                  (\partial_k)
                  \\right)
                  \\mathrm{d}x^k
                  \\,.
          %p Unwinding this with
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ad
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi j
                  %msubsup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo •
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (ad X)
                  \\;=\;
                  \\big(
                  x^j
                  f^\bullet_{j \bullet}
                  \\big)
                  \\,,
          %p
            (where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^i_{j k} \in \mathbb{R}
            denote the structure constants in the given basis, such that
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mi k
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X_j, X_k] = f^i_{j k} X_i
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mo −
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msubsup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi j
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi k
                  %mo +
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 6
                  %msubsup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                      %mo ′
                    %mi i
                  %msubsup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mi l
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ′
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi j
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi k
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi l
                  %mo +
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  e^i
                  \\;=\;
                  \\mathrm{d}x^i
                  \-
                  \\tfrac{1}{2}
                  f^i_{j k}x^j \mathrm{d}x^k
                  +
                  \\tfrac{1}{6}
                  f^i_{j k'}
                  f^{k'}_{k l}
                  x^j x^k \mathrm{d}x^l
                  +
                  \\cdots
                  \\,.
          %h2#OnInftyLieGroup
            On smooth
            = succeed "-groups" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            The theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
            embeds into the more general context of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
          %p
            for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-group"} smooth ∞-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \in Smooth\infty Grpd
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            there is canonically an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}G
            as described
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lie+infinity-groupoid#CoeffsLieAlgForms"} here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR}\mathbf{B}G
            correspond to flat
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            This fits into a double
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi θ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mo ♭
                            %mi dR
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mo ♭
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  G &amp;\to&amp; *
                  \\\
                  {}^{\mathllap{\theta}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}G &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{\flat} \mathbf{B}G
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  * &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p The morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\theta : G \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR}\mathbf{B}G
          %p
            in this diagram is the
            = succeed "-Maurer-Cartan" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            an ordinary Lie group, this reduces to the above definition. This statement and its proof is spelled out
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "smooth+infinity-groupoid+--+structures#CanonicalFormOnLieGroup"} here
          %h2#OnCohesiveHomotopyTypes On cohesive and stable homotopy types
          %h3#definition Definition
          %p
            Therefore generally for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \in \mathbf{H}
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            object, one may think of
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi fib
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ♭
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\theta \coloneqq fib(\flat \to \mathbf{B})
          %p
            as the Maurer-Cartan form on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            objects
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi G
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\theta_G \;\colon\; G \stackrel{}{\longrightarrow} \flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}G
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is discussed at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+infinity-topos+--+structures"} cohesive infinity-topos – structures
            in the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "cohesive+infinity-topos+--+structures#CurvatureCharacteristics"} Maurer-Cartan forms and curvature characteristics
          %p
            This includes then for instance Maurer-Cartan forms in higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            as discussed at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Super+Gerbes"} Super Gerbes
          %h3#properties_2 Properties
          %h4#relation_to_the_chern_character Relation to the Chern character
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"} stable homotopy type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape
            of the Maurer-Cartan form plays the role of the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            on
            = succeed "-cohomology." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
